 { In view of the chronic weakness on d5 White is better, but how to progress? } 1. { -KEY- } h3 $1 { Preparing g2-g4 with a new front on the kingside. } Ke6 ( { If } 1... h5 { , then } 2. g4 $1 { anyway, when at least one file is cleared for the rooks. } ) 
2. g4 Rh8 3. Rag1 fxg4 4. hxg4 ( { Another option was } 4. Bxg4 $5 f5 5. Bf3 { with h4-h5 next, in order to create a weakness on g6 - Roiz. } ) 
g5 $6 { Black enables ...Be8-g6, but 'don't move your pawns where you are weaker' goes an old saying. } ( { A safer choice was } 4... h6 { followed by ...Kf7-g7 - Roiz. } ) 
5. Rh6 Be8 6. Bh1 $1 { Preparing f2-f4 with increased pressure on Black. } ( 6. e4 dxe4 7. Bxe4 Bg6 8. Bxg6 Nxg6 9. Re1 Kf7 10. Nd5 Rcc8 { and Black keeps the material balance. } ) 
Bg6 7. f4 Be4 $2 { A tactical slip. } ( { Correct was } 7... Kf7 $1 8. c3 ( { not } 7... Be4 7. f5 $6 Kg7 { and 9... Bf7; } ) 
Kg7 9. Rh3 Be4 10. Bxe4 dxe4 { with an inferior, but materially balanced position. } ) 
8. fxg5 Ng8 9. Bxe4 dxe4 10. d5+ Kf7 ( { Or } 10... Ke5 11. Rf1 $1 Nxh6 12. gxh6 { with mate - Roiz. } ) 
11. g6+ $1 { Perhaps Black had overlooked this intermediate check, which preserves White's extra pawn. } Kg7 12. Rxh7+ Rxh7 13. gxh7 Kxh7 14. c4 $1 { Kharlov clears a path for his knight along c2-d4, and takes a first step in the future advance of the queenside pawn majority. } Kg6 15. Nc2 Nh6 16. Kc3 Nf7 ( { Or } 16... Rg7 17. Nd4 Kf7 18. Rh1 $1 { when both } Rg6 ( { and } 18... Nxg4 19. Nf5 ) 
19. Nf5 Nxf5 20. gxf5 { followed by Kd4, are terminal for Black - Roiz. } ) 
17. Nd4 Ne5 18. g5 $1 { A clever temporary sacrifice to activate the rook. } f5 ( { If } 18... fxg5 { then } 19. Ne6 Re7 ( { or } 19... Nf3 20. Rxg5 $1 Nxg5 21. Nxc7 Kf5 22. Ne6 $1 { heading for d8; } ) 
20. Rxg5 Kf6 21. Rg8 { with an overwhelming advantage. } ) 
19. Rh1 Ng4 20. Ne6 Rc8 ( { Or } 20... Re7 21. Rh8 Nxe3 22. Rh6 Kf7 23. Rh7 Ke8 24. g6 { etc - Roiz. } ) 
21. Rh3 Rb8 22. b4 b6 23. axb6 Rxb6 24. Rh8 Ne5 ( { If } 24... Nxe3 { then } 25. Rh6 Kf7 26. g6 { etc. } ) 
25. Rh6+ Kf7 26. Rf6+ ( { In view of his hopeless position after } 26. Rf6 Ke7 27. Nd4 { Black resigned. } ) 

